}+4{y}^{2}-12(0)+8y+4 & =0 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}+8y+4 & =0 \\\\ 4\\,[{y}^{2}+2y]+4 & =0 \\\\ 4[(y+1)^{2}-1]+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(y+1)^{2}-4+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(y+1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y+1 & =0 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,-1).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043117/assets/efaa5f474c5f505f6a1ca98469a77f8d21e059adee99c60cb9a2a7cb87600b5f.png)" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318842 13194139534907 true] [17592186318841 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534907 true] [17592186318841 1041 "field-1" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318841 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318842 13194139534907 true] [17592186318841 1110 #uuid "a42f2386-1e7d-5f17-afe5-e0ce3e45191b" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318842 1034 "0" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534907 true] [17592186318842 1111 #uuid "b17114f5-9be2-5607-814f-99024f980f92" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318843 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318844 13194139534907 true] [17592186318843 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534907 true] [17592186318843 1041 "field-2" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318843 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318844 13194139534907 true] [17592186318843 1110 #uuid "1b17dc1a-ebba-555d-99c1-4bf002eb6a57" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318844 1034 "-1" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534907 true] [17592186318844 1111 #uuid "d7b782f3-9ea3-5c24-a6a2-0a2c9a0898fb" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318845 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318846 13194139534907 true] [17592186318845 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318849 13194139534907 true] [17592186318845 1089 "q-327144" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318845 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534907 true] [17592186318845 1100 "Calculate the point where the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}-40x+100y+100=0$ intercepts the $y$-axis.\n\nThe $y$-intercept is $($\n{{field-1}}\n,\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318845 1113 #uuid "83504bae-41cf-56e1-be34-868e51df56b1" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318845 1145 "To calculate the $y$-intercept, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and try to solve the resulting equation for $y.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}-40x+100y+100 & =0 \\\\ 4(0)^{2}+25{y}^{2}-40(0)+100y+100 & =0 \\\\ 25{y}^{2}+100y+100 & =0 \\\\ 25\\,[{y}^{2}+4y+4] & =0 \\\\ 25\\,(y+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,-2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043117/assets/78be4ca7215ee8dbf05a442080bae752e4fadfbe76084d975338d00e1bb02c78.png)" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318846 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318847 13194139534907 true] [17592186318846 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318848 13194139534907 true] [17592186318846 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534907 true] [17592186318846 1041 "field-1" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318846 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318848 13194139534907 true] [17592186318846 1110 #uuid "d0fe0ded-7e43-5e65-b341-d71c3d415f42" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318847 1034 "1" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534907 true] [17592186318847 1111 #uuid "2b119996-3191-5522-91a2-c71d28bb06f1" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318848 1034 "0" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318848 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534907 true] [17592186318848 1111 #uuid "03f6b800-3d2d-5cd1-8610-d2263e984304" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318849 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318850 13194139534907 true] [17592186318849 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534907 true] [17592186318849 1041 "field-2" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318849 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318850 13194139534907 true] [17592186318849 1110 #uuid "813994d5-8190-5933-85c0-72fdde86b7c9" 13194139534907 true] [17592186318850 1034 "-2" 131941